< Prices of the list dated 2026-01-01: a cost belongs to that series only, and a new list or a change of `task-cycle/cycle_stages.py` starts a new one (WAY-339). A stretch of the orchestrator with no token usage costs nothing. A stage report whose section of stages has the columns *Cache write (5 minutes)* and *Cache write (1 hour)* is priced with each of them at its own price; an earlier form has its cache writes inside its input and prices them as input, an approximation. A cycle whose stage report has no section of stages is priced from its table of tokens by model at the same prices, and its share of the cost in fix rounds is unknown. *Fix rounds* is the number of findings files the record's *Review rounds* names; *Share of the cost in fix rounds* is the cost of the subagent turns given one of those findings files — each fix and the review of that fix — over the cycle's cost. `unknown` has its reason in *Unknown values*.
