< The versions are those of *Process versions*, but the series are not: the measures of how a cycle's agents use context and the prompt cache and the times of the gate are the numbers by which a change to the instructions of the cycle is judged, so only a change of the instrument that measures them splits them (WAY-339). A series of the mechanism measures begins at a version whose `task-cycle/cycle_measures.py` differs from the previous version's, and a series of the gate times at one whose `task-cycle/gate_times.py` or `gate/run_tests.py` differs, by `git diff --quiet` (exit 1, or any other failure, counts as changed). A new price list, a date of the register's list of classes and a change under `task-cycle/change`, `task-cycle/plan`, `task-cycle/review`, `task-cycle/spec` or of `task-cycle/cycle_stages.py` split neither, though a new price list and a change of `task-cycle/cycle_stages.py` split the series of the cost, and the others the series of the count of remarks. Each series is its own subsection, a number of one series is never set beside a number of another, and the cycles in no version stand in no series. *Falls* is `yes` where the median is lower than the previous version's median of the same measure in the same series, `no` where it is not, and `unknown` where the version is the first of its series or either median is not known; *Unknown values* says why. A median is written as the exact value, a half with its decimal.
